  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-08-24 (full text on WI-lutuh): \"yes — WI-lutuh is the long pole and needs scoping now; items 1-3 are prerequisites that make its output readable but don't substitute for it.\" This item is one of those three prerequisites, and the order the owner set is INV-juvul -> INV-rilit -> WI-nakut -> WI-lutuh scoping. The ruling also settles a scope question the project had never made explicitly: verify-claims IS meant to be usable on non-python repositories, which is what promotes WI-lutuh (14 of 15 catalogued languages declare ZERO module_completeness) from a rust footnote to the long pole."  # 42f1
- op: discuss  # dc33
  at: '2026-08-24T19:19:22Z'  # dc33
  by: agent  # dc33
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dc33
  clock: 3  # dc33
  nonce: dc33  # dc33
  message: "MEASURED AND FIXED 2026-08-24. Evidence, caches and both probes kept at\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/juvul_08242026/ (ab_probe.py runs BOTH arms in one\nprocess over the same cached survey and asserts the restore).\n\nRESULT, four unmodified upstream repos:\n\n  repo     lang  before  after  suppressed  verdicts\n  express  js    17      10     7           unchanged (all inconclusive)\n  bellman  rust  23      18     5           unchanged (all inconclusive)\n  caddy    go    160     158    2           unchanged (55/76/3, all violated)\n  httpx    py    41      41     0           unchanged\n\nNEWLY REPORTED is 0 on all four.\n\nTHREE MECHANISMS, not the two this item filed:\n  1. rust crate:: / super:: / self::  -- reserved words, exact.\n  2. js relative specifiers ./ ../    -- resolved against the importing file.\n  3. SEPARATOR ASYMMETRY, which this item did not name and which accounts for\n     express's lib/utils: _analyzed_modules folded / into . on the SRC side\n     while the callee side was compared RAW. That was a one-sided\n     implementation of a contract _module_matches already documented. The fold\n     now has ONE home (normalize_module_separators).\n\nTHE FIRST CUT WAS WRONG AND CADDY CAUGHT IT, before shipping. Folding the\nseparator and THEN running the existing prefix loop lets os/exec shorten to os\nand match caddy's own internal/filesystems/os.go. That cut suppressed 13\nmodules on caddy, TEN of them Go standard library -- crypto/ecdsa,\ncrypto/elliptic, crypto/hmac, crypto/md5, crypto/rand, crypto/sha256,\ncrypto/subtle, crypto/tls, crypto/x509, os/exec, os/signal. os/exec IS the\nsubprocess boundary. express and bellman looked CLEAN under that cut; only the\nGo repo showed it (LIVE.md rule 14). The shipped rule tests the folded spelling\nWHOLE and never shortens it.\n\nA SECOND DOCSTRING CLAIM OF MINE WAS ALSO WRONG AND WAS CORRECTED BY RUNNING\nIT: I wrote that a repo owning modules/caddyhttp would now suppress a\ndependency spelled github.com/other/modules/caddyhttp. It does not -- the\nfolded module is longer than the analyzed entry and the infix runs the other\nway. The real widening is exactly 2 entries on caddy, both caddy's own\npackages.\n\nCORRECTION TO THIS ITEM'S OWN ACCOUNT OF THE MECHANISM, relevant to INV-rilit:\nevery dotted rust entry here is a module_attr_ref edge whose \"module\" slot is a\nTYPE PATH, not a module path -- they are enum-variant and associated-constant\nreads:\n    rust:crate.SynthesisError:0-0:crate.SynthesisError.AssignmentMissing\n    rust:std.cmp.Ordering:0-0:std.cmp.Ordering.Greater\n    rust:ff.Field:0-0:ff.Field.ONE\n    rust:bellman.VerificationError:0-0:bellman.VerificationError.InvalidProof\nSo the dotted/colon split INV-rilit describes is not two spellings of one\nMODULE in these rows; it is a module path (calls, ::) versus a type path\n(module_attr_ref, .). That should be verified against INV-rilit's own fixture\nbefore its fix is designed.\n\nRESIDUALS FILED RATHER THAN GLOSSED:\n  INV-lakom (P1) prefix shortening is PRE-EXISTING for dotted languages and\n      still reproduces: a repo owning myapp/os/helpers.py and calling\n      os.path.join reports coverage COMPLETE over stdlib os. This change\n      declines to widen it; it does not close it.\n  INV-vivok (P3) a repo referring to itself by its PUBLISHED PACKAGE NAME\n      (bellman.VerificationError, github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2/...) is still\n      reported.\n\nTHE HONEST LIMIT, carried from this item into the PR unchanged: NO VERDICT\nFLIPPED. What remains is stdlib enumeration -- WI-lutuh."  # dc33
