  by: agent  # 8097
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8097
  clock: 5  # 8097
  nonce: '8097'  # 8097
  message: "MERGED as 2d8443df5e (PR #507). Re-run of this item's own repro ON THE MERGED\nTREE, with a positive control in the same run:\n\n  bellman  23 -> 18 modules, all three claims still inconclusive\n  express  17 -> 10 modules, all three claims still inconclusive\n  caddy    CONTROL: 55 net_send / 76 fs_write / 3 subprocess chains, all\n           three VIOLATED -- the tool still detects I/O in the same run\n  httpx    unchanged, 41 modules (measured pre-merge, 0 moved)\n\nNEWLY REPORTED is 0 on all four.\n\nNOT CLOSING THIS ITEM, and the reason is in its own statement. The statement\nnames THREE first-party spellings -- \"rust's crate::/super::/self:: keywords\nOR ITS OWN PACKAGE NAME, a javascript specifier beginning with . or /\". Two of\nthe three are closed with the evidence above. The third is NOT:\n`bellman.VerificationError` is still reported, and so are four\n`github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2/...` entries on caddy.\n\nMarking this satisfied would be a false closure on a clause I can read in the\nitem -- the INV-nufob failure mode -- so it stays violated, DEMOTED P1 -> P3 on\nmeasured size (1 of bellman's 18 remaining entries, 4 of caddy's 158; over-\nreporting is the SAFE direction, so what remains is noise, not a hole).\n\nThe remaining clause is now carried in full by INV-vivok, which is marked as\nblocking this item rather than duplicating it. INV-juvul closes when INV-vivok\ndoes.\n\nALSO FOUND WHILE MEASURING, filed separately because it is NOT this item:\nINV-lakom (P1) -- prefix shortening lets a repo owning `myapp/os/helpers.py`\nsuppress stdlib `os.path` entirely, reporting coverage COMPLETE. That is\nPRE-EXISTING for dotted languages. This fix deliberately declines to widen it\nto slash-spelled languages and pins the refusal, but does not close it."  # 8097
